      "writtenOn": "2022-09-20T17:22:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have thought about `-keep class * { native \u003cmethods\u003e; }`. But the potential problem is it may keep some native methods from the dependencies which might not be used by current target.  For example, ` android.net.connectivity.com.android.net.module.util.TcUtils` we need to keep the mative methods, but not native methods of different classes in the same package. So it would be helpful to specify the exact name here. \n\nFor only keeping the native methods. Yes, For tethering apk, we only keep the native methods of the corresponding classes, and leave the work for R8. For the standalone system server, the same opt passed the tests. What\u0027s more, I have compared the unused file between only keeping native methods and the entire classes, most of the differences are removing constants, few of them are methods, but these methods are not been called.",
      "parentUuid": "13ce84e6_946994c8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 2,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "4f5704a9e7608d4e9c93d6c19fdc7d7280811a3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d19bc39_22cc4558",
        "filename": "service/proguard.flags",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 2,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061164
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-20T18:16:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we have many native methods, and usually those always end up used in practice. If it becomes a problem eventually, module owners can specialize their keep rules further. I guess we are choosing between convenience and bloat in the apk here. And I don\u0027t think additional bloat in the case of native methods is significant enough to ask people to remember to add their specific classes here..\n\nBut ultimately, I\u0027d let Remi have a final say.. :-)\n\nOOC\u003c have you tried:\n\n-keepclasseswithmembernames,includedescriptorclasses class * {\n    native \u003cmethods\u003e;\n}\n\nor \n\n-keep class * { native }\n\n?",
      "parentUuid": "faf3e6f0_6dd18329",
      "range": {
